{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>When a man has, etc. — he does not hear.</b> One needs to understand the verse's saying <b>eineno</b> (\"he is not\"), for it should have said \"eno shome'a\" (\"he does not hear\"). Perhaps it comes to intimate that when a person enthrones the evil inclination within himself, awareness and hearing of what is said to him are stripped away from him, because the inclination stands at the entrance of the heart and prevents things from reaching the soul, since they would obligate him to depart from there. And I have compared the matter to a king whose gatekeepers were thieves and bandits — would it be possible for those gatekeepers to grant entry to those who come to lodge complaints before the king, so as to bring them before him? So too is this matter. And this is the meaning of His saying <b>When a man has</b>, etc., <b>he does not hear</b>, etc. — meaning, he is deprived, as it were, of the faculty of hearing, for the things do not reach him on account of the preventer who sits at the gates of the heart, as they said, of blessed memory (Berakhot 61a)." "<b>In the voice of his father and in the voice of his mother.</b> The reason it was necessary to mention \"his father\" and did not suffice to say \"in his voice,\" referring back to the father mentioned just above, is that the verse intimates that a wayward and rebellious son rebels against his progenitors — meaning, he rebels against his father and his mother, who are the Holy One, blessed be He, and Knesset Israel (Zohar vol. II, 85a), after the manner of what is said (Proverbs 1:8): ״שְׁמַע בְּנִי מוּסַר אָבִיךָ וְאַל תִּטֹּשׁ תּוֹרַת אִמֶּךָ״. For since his progenitors withhold their rod from their children and leave them to do what is good and upright in their own eyes, this brings it about that he rebels against them as well. And this is the measure of the verse <b>When a man has</b>, etc. — know that he does not hear the voice of the Holy One, blessed be He, and Knesset Israel; and therefore even though they discipline him he will not heed them — meaning, not only will he not accept correction to turn back from the transgressions between him and the Place (i.e. HaShem), but furthermore he will not heed them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:18:26.454647746Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}